This fixture is DISTRIBUTION-ONLY. It must never be copied to a consumer.

It is shard 'b' of advisor-gate-deny-mutants, and it inherits that fixture's reason without
restating it: it is the MUTATION BATTERY behind the shipped advisor-gate-deny fixture, editing
copies of core's own hook in temp trees, so every verdict is a question about whether THIS
repository's hook still discriminates.

A shard is a scheduling boundary, never a subject boundary, so it can carry no ship decision
its sibling does not. On a consumer it would be a unit the consumer cannot act on, sitting in
that consumer's suite schedule.
